    description: "Source: deep-20260407-030917 prometheus reflect agent. Closure-wrapped handlers are still erased from the call graph: r.Post('/read', api.ready(api.remoteRead)) produces a routes_to -> api.remoteRead edge but the 'ready' middleware wrapper is invisible. Same for 'wrap', 'wrapAgent' wrappers in web/api/v1/api.go:425-484. For middleware/auth refactoring, the wrap layer is invisible — the route resolver fix (INV-kunam) doesn't help because wrap isn't modeled at all. Fix: when a route registration call passes a closure call expression as its handler argument, model the inner function as a wrapping/decorating call edge with a wraps or middleware_of edge type. This is distinct from the closed WI-hosad work which added middleware concepts to entrypoint mapping but did not link them to the wrapped handler chain."  # 2e65
    fields: {}  # 2e65
